            <ArticleTitle>A 19-Year-Old College Student With Headache, Photophobia, and Flulike Illness.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e95-e98</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0012-3692(16)62335-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.chest.2016.10.047</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE PRESENTATION" NlmCategory="METHODS">A 19-year-old previously healthy man presented, minimally responsive, in respiratory distress to an ED after a 2-week history of headache, photophobia, and neck stiffness. Associated symptoms included low-grade fevers, malaise, and dark urine. He had no recent travel, ill contacts, consumption of undercooked meat, new sexual contacts, or illicit drug use. The patient resided in a campus dormitory and did not consume alcohol or tobacco.</AbstractText>
